<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marmarica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marmarica is the ancient name for the coastal plateau and desert between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, in modern north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>. It was home to Libyan pastoral peoples whom Greek and Roman writers called the Marmaridae. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> it was attached at first to Cyrenaica and later formed the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya-inferior">Libya Inferior</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marmarica.jpg" alt="Marmarica" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastian Münster · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BCnster_Aphricae_Tabula_III_1540_UTA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
